eer, including his consulship, took place within the institutional framework of the Roman Republic."}, {"sourceSlug": "lucius-fulvius-curvus", "sourceName": "Lucius Fulvius Curvus", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "gens-fulvia", "targetName": "Gens Fulvia", "context": "His consulship in 322 BCE definitively established the *gens Fulvia* as a major aristocratic family in Roman politics for centuries to come."}], "places": [{"name": "Rome, Italy", "role": "Center of political career"}, {"name": "Samnium, Italy", "role": "Major military theater"}, {"name": "Fratte, Italy", "role": "Site of military victory"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Lucius Fulvius Curvus", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "lucius-fulvius-curvus"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1146364", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucius_Fulvius_Curvus"], "tags": ["Military Leaders & Commanders", "conflict-and-resolution", "geopolitical-linkage", "temporal-linkage"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 6, "significanceNarrative": "Lucius Fulvius Curvus's consulship and military successes were crucial in establishing the *gens Fulvia* as a leading Roman family and contributed to Rome's consolidation of power in central Italy during a critical phase of its expansion.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-09-13T07:00:13Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#34742798840", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Lucius Fulvius Curvus was an aristocrat of the middle Roman Republic and consul prior in 322 BC with Quintus Fabius Maximus Rullianus. He is the first of the gens Fulvia documented in the history of Rome.", "newValue": "Lucius Fulvius Curvus, an aristocrat of the early Roman Republic, holds historical significance as the first documented member of the distinguished *gens Fulvia* to achieve the consulship. His election as consul *prior* in 322 BCE, alongside Quintus Fabius Maximus Rullianus, was a pivotal moment not only for his family's nascent political prominence but also for the ongoing consolidation of Roman power during the intense Third Samnite War. His career exemplifies the martial and political ambitions characteristic of Rome's expanding elite in the late 4th century BCE, laying the groundwork for one of the Republic's most influential families.

During his consulship in 322 BCE, Lucius Fulvius Curvus led Roman legions against the tenacious Samnites, a conflict crucial for Rome's dominance in central Italy. He is credited with a significant victory near Fratte (ancient Fruentium), where his forces decisively defeated a Samnite army, capturing their camp and a substantial quantity of supplies. This military success was instrumental in weakening Samnite resistance and bolstering Roman morale. Following this triumph, the Roman Senate granted him a *triumph*, a public procession celebrating his victory, which further cemented his prestige and the growing military might of the Republic.

Curvus's consulship established a powerful precedent for the *gens Fulvia*, elevating them from relative obscurity to a position within the highest echelons of Roman society. His descendants would continue to play crucial roles in Roman politics and military affairs for centuries. Notable among them were figures like Quintus Fulvius Flaccus, a four-time consul and general during the Punic Wars, and Marcus Fulvius Nobilior, who famously conquered Ambracia in Greece. The Fulvii's consistent presence in the consular fasti and their participation in key historical events directly stemmed from the foundational political achievement of Lucius Fulvius Curvus."}, {"timestamp": "2026-09-13T07:00:13Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#34742798840", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Classical era: flourishing of philosophical inquiry, imperial expansion, and codification of la", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "355 BCE, Ancient Rome"}, {"title": "Military conflicts and strategic necessities", "type": "Idea", "year": "355 BCE, Ancient Rome"}], "newValue": ["The ongoing expansionist ambitions of the early Roman Republic necessitated competent military and political leadership.", "The strategic importance of the Samnite Wars created opportunities for military distinction and political advancement.", "The established system of elected magistracies in the Roman Republic allowed ambitious aristocrats to achieve high office."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-09-13T07:00:13Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#34742798840", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Determined military outcomes shaping geopolitical boundaries", "type": "Idea", "year": "360 BCE"}, {"title": "Contributed to enduring intellectual and institutional frameworks shaping subsequent civilizati", "type": "Movement", "year": "360 BCE"}], "newValue": ["Lucius Fulvius Curvus's consulship established the *gens Fulvia* as a prominent and enduring force in Roman aristocratic politics.", "His military victory contributed to the Roman Republic's consolidation of power and territorial control during the Third Samnite War.", "The precedent set by his achievement encouraged future generations of the Fulvian family to pursue public office and military glory."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-09-13T07:00:13Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#34742798840", "field": "detailsJson.relationships", "oldValue": [{"sourceSlug": "lucius-fulvius-curvus", "sourceName": "Lucius Fulvius Curvus", "verb": "COMMANDS", "targetSlug": "field-280", "targetName": "Military Leaders & Commanders", "context": "Lucius Fulvius Curvus: Military command in military leaders & commanders"}, {"sourceSlug": "lucius-fulvius-curvus", "sourceName": "Lucius Fulvius Curvus", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "classical", "targetName": "Classical Era", "context": "Lucius Fulvius Curvus was active during the Classical era"}], "newValue": [{"sourceSlug": "roman-electoral-system", "sourceName": "Roman Electoral System", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "lucius-fulvius-curvus", "targetName": "Lucius Fulvius Curvus", "context": "Lucius Fulvius Curvus's ascent to the consulship in 322 BCE was a direct outcome of the Roman Republic's electoral processes."}, {"sourceSlug": "lucius-fulvius-curvus", "sourceName": "Lucius Fulvius Curvus", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "third-samnite-war", "targetName": "Third Samnite War", "context": "He commanded Roman forces during the Third Samnite War in 322 BCE, securing a significant victory against the Samnites."}, {"sourceSlug": "lucius-fulvius-curvus", "sourceName": "Lucius Fulvius Curvus", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "quintus-fabius-maximus-rullianus", "targetName": "Quintus Fabius Maximus Rullianus", "context": "They served as co-consuls for the Roman Republic in 322 BCE, jointly overseeing state and military affairs."}, {"sourceSlug": "lucius-fulvius-curvus", "sourceName": "Lucius Fulvius Curvus", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targ